./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2864:The decorated-recursion build is landing cleanly (spine + measure bedrock + the invariant's arithmetic core + the base's Rayleigh core all in canonical, clean-three), and the analysis has isolated the *single* remaining piece that may force a Proved-vs-Cited choice — the kind you were strict about (#97: build the (S,J) core, don't cite). It's the "incidence" step: passing one layer deeper, the codimension jumps by enough that the collapsing block stays transverse (this is what makes the recursion's invariant hold). The **math is certified** (the auditor's #144, decorrelated + second-model). The question is purely *formalization*: stating it in Lean the direct way needs algebraic-geometry infrastructure Mathlib lacks (irreducible-component decomposition + generic rank on a component) — a large build, possibly a wall. **Two options:** (α) build that AG infrastructure — honors "don't cite," but expensive/uncertain; (β) carry the one fact ("deeper rank ≥ b") as a certified *interface* — exactly analogous to how we already carry the Aoyagi rlct=½codim step — cheap, but it *cites* a geometric step, against the letter of #97. **I am NOT deciding this by fiat, and NOT surfacing it prematurely:** first the auditor (who owns the geometry) is checking whether there's a *native* Lean re-expression that sidesteps the AG infrastructure entirely (via the banked codimension arithmetic + an elementary determinantal bound) — the "re-express, don't wall" move. If a native route exists → (α) becomes bounded labour and I just build it, no decision needed. **Only if it's a genuine formalization-wall will I bring you the α-cost-vs-β-cite call** — because β contradicts #97 and that's yours, not mine. Flagging now so it's not a surprise; the build continues above the gap meanwhile (the fact is carried as a named hypothesis, so everything else lands and this plugs in when resolved). No action yet.
./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2866:**#114 RESOLVED (2026-07-11): (i) is native — build it, no citation, no decision needed from you.** The auditor's decorrelated assessment (+ second model + exact verification) found the "re-express, don't wall" route: the incidence fact reduces to a single elementary finite-minimum identity (a reindexing of the banked codimension formula — "peeling from the back"), which sidesteps the algebraic-geometry infrastructure entirely. No irreducible-component/generic-rank machinery needed. So it's **bounded labour, built for real** — the operator's "don't cite the (S,J) core" (#97) is honored at modest cost, and there's **no Proved-vs-Cited decision to bring you**. This is the disposition paying off again: "possibly a wall" was not a wall; attempting the native re-expression dissolved it. (One honest correction rode along: the auditor retracted an earlier glib "higher codimension ⟹ automatic margin" — a counterexample shows higher codim can carry a *lower* RLCT — so the deficient-rank/intersection neighbourhoods are genuine coupled work for the decorated descent, not a free consequence. No scope change: those rays are already certified at the two anchors, and the width-general case was always the decorated descent's job.)
./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/discuss-at-close.md:2871:Building the base leg surfaced — and two decorrelated passes confirmed — that the admissibility predicate as first designed is too weak to PROVE the base finite. The formaliser found (and the auditor + adversarial Codex confirmed) that an adversarial admissible carrier can diverge: the predicate doesn't bound the carrier's monomial threshold, and the base is really a *coupled* integral (the deeper residuals vanish over the parameter box), not the pure-monomial terminal a first reading assumed. This is the SAME theme as the auditor's earlier "d=0 degenerate" flag, now at bigger scope (d≥1 too). It does NOT break the result (extra admitted decorations only *strengthen* the ∀-obligation; specialising at the trivial decoration still gives the correct finiteness fact) — but it means the base hypothesis must be genuinely PROVED, never postulated (a divergent admitted decoration would make it FALSE → postulating it would be an unsound false-hypothesis gap). The formaliser correctly REFUSED to force or postulate it — the bedrock bar held, on the leg that is audited hardest. **Resolution (auditor + decorrelated Codex converge): the predicate carries a bundled "faithful (S,J) resolution-state" invariant** — normal-crossings form + the ½·codim threshold + a *quantitative* residual-coercivity (Codex caught that a mere null-zero-set is insufficient — a vanishing residual still diverges the negative moment) — all of which is the (S,J) resolution's OWN content, matching the already-certified step machinery. The base CONSUMES the invariant; the step PRESERVES it. This RE-COUPLES the recursion's base and step around one invariant — the earlier "the valuation predicate decouples #3 from #5" was over-optimistic; the coupling is *intrinsic* to a decorated induction (a decorated IH necessarily reaches the base with arbitrary decorated states, which must be constrained to faithful ones through the predicate). But it CONSOLIDAT